{
  "workflowId": "300000331058399",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_FIN_FA_RETIREMENT_REQUEST_ASSISTANT",
  "name": "Retirement Request Assistant",
  "description": "Allows users to submit fixed asset retirement requests for individual assets or groups of assets under their responsibility. The request is routed to the asset accountant for processing, and status can be monitored throughout the lifecycle until it is posted.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778578652558"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Read User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771838992651"
          },
          "code": "READ_USER_INTENT",
          "id": "1769876808561",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769876808562_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "From the input message {{$context.$variables.currentInput}}, determine the userIntent.\n\nReturn ONLY the userIntent value.\n\nMatch case-insensitively and ignore leading/trailing whitespace.\nEvaluate priorities in order and stop at the first matching rule.\n\nAllowed userIntent values:\n- HELP\n- TERMINATE_TRANSACTION\n- UPDATE_RETIREMENT_DATA\n- PROCESS_RETIREMENT\n- RETIRE_OWNED_ASSETS\n- GET_MY_ASSETS\n- OWNED_ASSETS_RET_REQUESTS\n- OTHER_QUESTIONS\n\nPRIORITY 1 — Fetched user assets flow\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.requestState}} is \"FETCHED_USER_ASSETS\", then apply these rules.\n\n1) If {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} contains an update/change/edit/modify/correct/revise/adjust/set/replace command\n   and mentions any of these fields:\n   - retire date\n   - retirement date\n   - retirement reason\n   - reason\n   - comment\n   - comments\n\n   then return:\n\n   UPDATE_RETIREMENT_DATA\n\n2) Else if {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} is exactly or primarily a row reference, ordinal selection, asset identifier, or selection command, such as:\n   - row 1\n   - row 2\n   - rows 1 and 2\n   - first\n   - second\n   - first one\n   - second one\n   - select row 1\n   - select the first one\n   - TG_107581\n   - 107581\n   - ASSET12345\n   - select TG_107581\n   - retire TG_107581\n   - process TG_107581\n   - these\n   - them\n   - the assets\n   - all rows\n   - every row\n   - select all\n   - all of them\n   - continue\n   - process\n   - submit\n   - retire these\n   - retire them\n   - retire all\n\n   then return:\n\n   RETIRE_OWNED_ASSETS\n\n3) Else if {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} generally asks to fetch, show, list, view, or retire the user's own assets, such as:\n   - retire my assets\n   - retire assets assigned to me\n   - show my assets\n   - list my assets\n   - fetch my assets\n   - view my assets\n\n   then return:\n\n   GET_MY_ASSETS\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not route to RETIRE_OWNED_ASSETS when the message is an update to retirement data.\n- If the message contains both row selection language and update/change/edit language for retirement fields, return UPDATE_RETIREMENT_DATA.\n\nPRIORITY 2 — Prepared retirement flow\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.requestState}} is any of:\n- \"PREPARED_OWNED_ASSETS_RETIREMENT_DATA\"\n- \"PREPARED_OTHER_ASSETS_RETIREMENT_DATA\"\n- \"RETIREMENT_DATA_UPDATED\"\n- \"READY_TO_SUBMIT\"\n\nand {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} contains an update/change/edit command such as:\n- update\n- change\n- modify\n- edit\n- correct\n- revise\n- adjust\n- set\n- replace\n\nand mentions any of these fields:\n- retire date\n- retirement date\n- retirement reason\n- reason\n- comment\n- comments\n\nthen return:\n\nUPDATE_RETIREMENT_DATA\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} directly assigns a value to one of those fields, such as:\n- comments should say damaged\n- reason should be duplicate asset\n- retirement date should be tomorrow\n\nthen return:\n\nUPDATE_RETIREMENT_DATA\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} asks to show, view, display, or provide retirement details, retirement data, retirement information, or retirement fields such as retire date, retirement reason, or comments, then return:\n\nUPDATE_RETIREMENT_DATA\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.requestState}} is \"READY_TO_SUBMIT\"\nand {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} confirms, approves, submits, or agrees to proceed, such as:\n- yes\n- y\n- yeah\n- yep\n- ok\n- okay\n- sure\n- proceed\n- continue\n- submit\n- confirm\n- approved\n- go ahead\n- sounds good\n- that's correct\n\nthen return:\n\nPROCESS_RETIREMENT\n\nPRIORITY 3 — Attachment-based retirement\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.requestState}} is not one of:\n- \"PREPARED_OWNED_ASSETS_RETIREMENT_DATA\"\n- \"PREPARED_OTHER_ASSETS_RETIREMENT_DATA\"\n- \"RETIREMENT_DATA_UPDATED\"\n- \"READY_TO_SUBMIT\"\n- \"FETCHED_USER_ASSETS\"\n\nand {{$context.$variables.isAttachmentAdded}} is true or equals \"true\"\n\nand {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} references an attachment, file, sheet, spreadsheet, or attached data,\nor asks to process, submit, proceed, continue, retire, update, review, or use the attached file,\n\nthen return:\n\nOTHER_QUESTIONS\n\nPRIORITY 4 — Fresh intent\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.requestState}} is empty or null\nand the user asks to retire an asset using a tag number, serial number, asset number, or other unique asset identifier,\n\nthen return:\n\nOTHER_QUESTIONS\n\nIf the user asks for unit retirement, source line retirement, or reinstatement,\n\nthen return:\n\nOTHER_QUESTIONS\n\nIf the user asks:\n- retire my assets\n- retire assets assigned to me\n- show my assets\n- list my assets\n- fetch my assets\n- view my assets\n\nthen return:\n\nGET_MY_ASSETS\n\nIf the user asks to review, show, list, or view retirement requests created by him,\n\nthen return:\n\nOWNED_ASSETS_RET_REQUESTS\n\nIf the user asks to retire other assets not assigned to him without giving asset details,\n\nthen return:\n\nOTHER_QUESTIONS\n\nPRIORITY 5 — Cancellation / termination\n\nIf {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} clearly cancels or abandons the current transaction, such as:\n- cancel\n- cancel request\n- cancel this\n- stop\n- terminate\n- abort\n- never mind\n- forget it\n- do not proceed\n- don't proceed\n- discontinue\n\nthen return:\n\nTERMINATE_TRANSACTION\n\nPRIORITY 6 — Help\n\nReturn HELP if {{$context.$variables.currentInput}} explicitly asks for help, instructions, guidance, explanations, documentation, valid retirement reasons, allowed retirement reasons, detailed validations related to asset retirement, validation errors, validation messages, or asks to display/show validation messages, such as:\n- help\n- help me\n- how do I retire an asset\n- how can I submit retirement\n- what should I do\n- guide me\n- instructions\n- explain how asset retirement works\n- valid retirement reasons\n- allowed retirement reasons\n- what reasons are allowed for retirement\n- what are valid reasons to retire an asset\n- what retirement reasons can I use\n- acceptable retirement reasons\n- list retirement reasons\n- show retirement reasons\n- available retirement reasons\n- retirement reason options\n- what should I select as retirement reason\n- which retirement reason should I choose\n- explain retirement reasons\n- retirement reason help\n- validation errors\n- validation error\n- show validation errors\n- display validation errors\n- what are the validation errors\n- explain validation errors\n- validation messages\n- show validation messages\n- display validation messages\n- explain validation messages\n- help with validation errors\n- help with validation messages\n- validation error\n- validation errors\n- validation message\n- validation messages\n\n\nIf the user asks for help about unrelated topics such as coding, JavaScript, debugging, or general support, then return:\n\nOTHER_QUESTIONS\n\nIf no rule matches,\n\nthen return:\n\nOTHER_QUESTIONS"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"userIntent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
